<!--
  Hub studio · `/studio/components` — the component catalog index.

  Composes the `@ship/studio` pack's <ship-component-catalog>, which
  owns the catalog data story (BACKEND-GAP today; the empty-state
  explains the gap + flags the operator-visible
  `.artifacts/hub-buildout-flags.md` entry). The route is a thin
  composition — chrome is the root layout, the page body is the pack
  component.

  Top chrome: the <ship-nav-top> is owned by the root layout
  (`routes/_layout.sui` → `<ship-app-chrome>`). The breadcrumb trail
  auto-derives from `location.pathname` and shows
  `/studio/components`.

  Per the hub-buildout-charter §Connect-only, the catalog needs a
  `ship.ui.components.list()` op that does not exist today (no Connect
  surface; the shell's HTTP catalog was purged; the framework stopped
  writing the .deck/catalogs/workspace.json index). The component
  degrades to the documented empty-state — no invented data, no
  resurrected fetch.
-->
<main class="studio-components">
  <ship-component-catalog></ship-component-catalog>
</main>
